T GlyphSpecification                     | VectorInterchange.h | 173-180 | owning          | -  | One glyph — its outline, and the metrics that position it. The character string is stored beside it so the text stays editable. Storing only characters means every resolution re-runs substitution, and substitution depends on the typeface — so replacing a typeface silently changes the shaping of text the artist already positioned.
    has   GlyphIdentity  std::uint32_t             [-]  ?
    has   Paths          std::vector<OutlinePath>  [-]  ?
    has   Advance        double                    [-]  ?
    has   BearingAlong   double                    [-]  ?
    has   BearingAcross  double                    [-]  ?
    by    Api/TypefaceCodec.h, Source/AnalyticProjection.cpp, Source/ConsoleHost.cpp, Source/TypefaceCodec.cpp, Source/VectorInterchange.cpp
    note  🔴 `52` §3: text is resolved to a **glyph sequence** at intake and the glyph sequence is what is stored.

